body:
Hi, I gave a look but I didn't get far unfortunately.

Near the end of the logs there are these entries when attempting to copy:

> Couldn't set selection, seat doesn't have wl_data_device.

> Couldn't set primary selection, seat doesn't have wp_primary_selection_device.

The protocol dumps are all tangled up with the running game unfortunately, but it looks like the respective objects are indeed initialized so I have absolutely no idea on how this could happen.

Perhaps the current seat gets overridden, I'm genuinely unsure.

Curiosly I actually got a similar random issue with primary selection in my embedder but I couldn't pinpoint what was going on there either.

Hopefully the below patch could help you getting more detailed info (run with `--verbose`):

```patch
diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
index 07fade1441..3e156ac57a 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
@@ -305,6 +305,8 @@ void WaylandThread::_set_current_seat(struct wl_seat *p_seat) {
 		return;
 	}

+	DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD(vformat("Setting current seat to wl_seat#%d.", wl_proxy_get_id((wl_proxy *)p_seat)));
+
 	SeatState *old_state = wl_seat_get_seat_state(wl_seat_current);

 	if (old_state) {
@@ -461,6 +463,7 @@ void WaylandThread::_wl_registry_on_global(void *data, struct wl_registry *wl_re
 			ERR_FAIL_NULL(ss);

 			if (ss->wl_data_device == nullptr) {
+				DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD(vformat("Initializing data device for wl_seat#%d.", wl_proxy_get_id((wl_proxy *)wl_seat)));
 				ss->wl_data_device = wl_data_device_manager_get_data_device(registry->wl_data_device_manager, wl_seat);
 				wl_data_device_add_listener(ss->wl_data_device, &wl_data_device_listener, ss);
 			}
@@ -501,12 +504,14 @@ void WaylandThread::_wl_registry_on_global(void *data, struct wl_registry *wl_re
 		// NOTE: Don't forget to also bind/destroy with the respective global.
 		if (!ss->wl_data_device && registry->wl_data_device_manager) {
 			// Clipboard & DnD.
+			DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD(vformat("Initializing data device for wl_seat#%d.", wl_proxy_get_id((wl_proxy *)wl_seat)));
 			ss->wl_data_device = wl_data_device_manager_get_data_device(registry->wl_data_device_manager, wl_seat);
 			wl_data_device_add_listener(ss->wl_data_device, &wl_data_device_listener, ss);
 		}

 		if (!ss->wp_primary_selection_device && registry->wp_primary_selection_device_manager) {
 			// Primary selection.
+			DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD(vformat("Initializing primary data device for wl_seat#%d.", wl_proxy_get_id((wl_proxy *)wl_seat)));
 			ss->wp_primary_selection_device = zwp_primary_selection_device_manager_v1_get_device(registry->wp_primary_selection_device_manager, wl_seat);
 			zwp_primary_selection_device_v1_add_listener(ss->wp_primary_selection_device, &wp_primary_selection_device_listener, ss);
 		}
@@ -589,6 +594,7 @@ void WaylandThread::_wl_registry_on_global(void *data, struct wl_registry *wl_re
 			ERR_FAIL_NULL(ss);

 			if (!ss->wp_primary_selection_device && registry->wp_primary_selection_device_manager) {
+				DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD(vformat("Initializing primary data device for wl_seat#%d.", wl_proxy_get_id((wl_proxy *)wl_seat)));
 				ss->wp_primary_selection_device = zwp_primary_selection_device_manager_v1_get_device(registry->wp_primary_selection_device_manager, wl_seat);
 				zwp_primary_selection_device_v1_add_listener(ss->wp_primary_selection_device, &wp_primary_selection_device_listener, ss);
 			}
@@ -4577,7 +4583,7 @@ void WaylandThread::selection_set_text(const String &p_text) {
 	}

 	if (ss->wl_data_device == nullptr) {
-		DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD("Couldn't set selection, seat doesn't have wl_data_device.");
+		DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD(vformat("Couldn't set selection, wl_seat#%d doesn't have wl_data_device.", wl_proxy_get_id((wl_proxy *)wl_seat_current)));
 		return;
 	}

@@ -4698,7 +4704,7 @@ void WaylandThread::primary_set_text(const String &p_text) {
 	}

 	if (ss->wp_primary_selection_device == nullptr) {
-		DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD("Couldn't set primary selection, seat doesn't have wp_primary_selection_device.");
+		DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND_THREAD(vformat("Couldn't set primary selection, wl_seat#%d doesn't have wp_primary_selection_device.", wl_proxy_get_id((wl_proxy *)wl_seat_current)));
 		return;
 	}

```

@Cykyrios no worries, thank you for being so determined to help! The data you sent is exactly what I was talking about but unfortunately it's perfect :(

Let's take a step back and let me ask you about your setup: what distro/compositor are you currently using? Any particular i/o peripherals (especially while developing)? Lastly, could you install the `wayland-utils` package and send me the output of `wayland-info`? Maybe there are multiple seats or a compositor quirk that we aren't handling correctly.

(Regarding wayland-info, it doesn't tell necessarily new stuff but it does its best to pretty-print it. Maybe I'm missing something from the crowded logs.)
